":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1533,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current code (fetcher.py:561-583): a single shared `seen_keys` set + one `if key in seen_keys: alert_store.append({'kind': 'fetcher-dedup-suppressed', ...})` branch covers cross-page, cross-query (active vs done-recent) AND cross-project duplicates.","A per-project LOCAL dict keyed by issue key would let a within-project cross-query duplicate overwrite silently, so its dedup alert is only emitted if the local drain itself tracks a seen set / consults shared seen_keys during the drain — the plan does not state this.","Plan phrase 'dedup now runs at the atomic merge' addresses cross-project dedup at merge time but not the pre-merge intra-project cross-query dupe."],"finding":"The plan's dedup-preservation claim is under-specified for the intra-project cross-query duplicate: draining both base queries into a per-project LOCAL dict before merge can silently drop the fetcher-dedup-suppressed alert that the current shared seen_keys loop emits for an active-vs-done-recent duplicate within one project.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f78725c0f8348886d","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'Keep the dedup (seen_keys) and the fetcher-dedup-suppressed alert behavior intact — dedup now runs at the atomic merge of each project's local dict.'","norm_id":"n2970bc61f32fe3a4","priority":0.4467,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A project whose active and done-recent queries both return the same issue key (the tolerated-but-abnormal cross-query dupe the docstring at fetcher.py:495-498 exists to handle) — the dedup-suppressed alert stops firing."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Have _fetch_project take (or consult) the shared seen_keys during its two-query drain and emit fetcher-dedup-suppressed on a dupe exactly as today, adding keys to seen_keys only when the project's local dict is committed on success (rollback on failure); state this explicitly in the Approach.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the positive rationale for fail-open whole-project discard grounded in the real mechanism (ADR 0028: absence routes to a bounded PROBE_GET with grace, not a deletion; the blast-radius breake